Subject: [sshmap fork 0002] LNM (mode 20) enabled by default

Provenance: sshmap — PYTE82_AUDIT.md patch A2 (implemented in v1.2.11 as the
            SshmapHistoryScreen __init__/reset overrides, moved to the fork in
            v1.3rc1). One line: _DEFAULT_MODE gains mo.LNM — bare LF = CR+LF
            (xterm behavior; real terminals keep LNM on). Screen.reset() restores
            mode = _DEFAULT_MODE.copy(), so this one line covers BOTH the
            constructor and the RIS (ESC c) path. Explicit SM/RM 20 from a remote
            program still works as before.
Base:       pyte 0.8.2, pyte/screens.py (_DEFAULT_MODE).
Policy:     keep until upstream ships LNM-by-default; then drop.
Applied:    2026-09-10, sshmap v1.3rc1.

diff --git a/pyte/screens.py b/pyte/screens.py
--- a/pyte/screens.py
+++ b/pyte/screens.py
@@ -134,7 +134,7 @@
         return self.default
 
 
-_DEFAULT_MODE = set([mo.DECAWM, mo.DECTCEM])
+_DEFAULT_MODE = set([mo.DECAWM, mo.DECTCEM, mo.LNM])
 
 
 class Screen:
